``` T1486 — symmetric GPG encryption (gpg -c with a passphrase on the command line), port of elastic.esql ```
``` Uses EXECVE records (a0..aN) instead of PROCTITLE, which auditd stores hex-encoded. Draft: validate against your linux_audit output. ```
index=linux sourcetype=linux_audit type=EXECVE (a0="gpg" OR a0="*/gpg") "passphrase"
| rex max_match=0 "\sa\d+=\"?(?<arg>[^\"\s]+)"
| where isnotnull(mvfind(arg, "^(-c|--symmetric)$")) AND isnotnull(mvfind(arg, "passphrase"))
| eval cmdline=mvjoin(arg, " ")
| stats count as encrypted_files min(_time) as first_event max(_time) as last_event values(cmdline) as targets by host
| eval duration_sec=last_event-first_event, mitre_technique="T1486 - Data Encrypted for Impact"
| where encrypted_files>=2
| convert ctime(first_event) ctime(last_event)
| sort - encrypted_files
